.TH SDL_PauseHaptic 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_PauseHaptic \- Pause a haptic device.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_haptic.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_PauseHaptic(SDL_Haptic *haptic);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Device must support the
.BR SDL_HAPTIC_PAUSE
feature\[char46] Call
.BR SDL_ResumeHaptic ()
to resume playback\[char46]
.PP
Do not modify the effects nor add new ones while the device is paused\[char46] That can cause all sorts of weird errors\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I haptic
the
.BR SDL_Haptic
device to pause\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_ResumeHaptic (3)
